  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="61">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 61</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="61" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>[G]if<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_61.lnote.oe.4"/> hwa on fyrde gryðbryce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_61.lnote.oe.13"/> fulwyrce, ðolige lifes oððe weregildes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="61" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Griðbryce. Gyf hwa on fyrde griðbryce fulwyrce, ðolie liues oððon weregyldes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="61" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="350" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa on fyrde griðbrice fulwyrce, þolige lifes oððe wæregildes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="61" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in exercitu (regis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_61.lnote.oe.17"/>) pacis infractionem perficiat, uitam perdat uel wéregildo redimat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="61" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis in bello pacem fregerit, quod Angli dicunt griþbrece<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_61.lnote.oe.16"/>, reus est mortis aut prętii sui.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#IICn_61.lnote.oe.17-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="61" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>[61] Si quis in exercitu pacem plene fregerit, amittat uitam uel uite (dignitatem, scilicet) redempcionem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="61" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="204" ed="#robertson"/>Griðbryce. Gyf hwa on fyrde griðbryce fulwyrce, ðolie liues oððon weregyldes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="284" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif hwa on fyrde gryðbryce fulwyrce, ðolige lifes oððe weregildes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="351" ed="#liebermann"/>(Bruch des Sonderfriedens. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_61.lnote.de.1"/> einer in der Landwehr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_61.lnote.de.2"/> Bruch des Sonderfriedens voll[schwer, durch Todtschlag<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_61.lnote.de.3"/>] verübt, verliere er Leben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_61.lnote.de.4"/> oder [sein] Wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Breach of special peace. B) If anyone commits a full[-weight] breach of special peace [by homicide] in the army, let him lose life or [his] wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="205" ed="#robertson"/>Breach of the peace. If anyone is guilty of a capital deed of violence<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_61.robnote.n.1"/> while serving in the army, he shall lose his life or his wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="471" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone commits a full breach of the peace in the army, he is to forfeit his life or his wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="285" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone commits a capital crime while serving in the army, he shall lose either his life or his wergild.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 351, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Griðbryce</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">Gif: if with space for the initial in G</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">pleno pa. infreg. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">pleno pa. infreg. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">aut <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">aut Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d. s. <hi rend="italic">nur Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d. s. only Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus Dm THk; fehlt KRHn</hi> 13, 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from Dm THk; lacking in KRHn 13, 8</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">if, <hi rend="italic">davor Raum für</hi> [<hi rend="italic">farbige</hi>] <hi rend="italic">Initiale G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">if, with space before it for the [coloured] initial G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">350</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">griþbrece <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">griþbrece Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-che <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-che Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.oe.17-2" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">351</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">61, 1 <hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">61, 1 lacking</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 13, 8 und aus Inst durch Ps Cn for 18. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Heer 6a. 7. Auch Nordisches Recht scheidet im Heerfrieden Totschlag von anderer Missetat; Wilda <hi rend="italic">Strafr</hi>. 240</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 13, 8 and, from Inst, by Ps Cn for 18. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Heer 6a. 7. Norse law too distinguishes, within the peace of the army, homicide from other misdeeds; Wilda <hi rend="italic">Strafr</hi>. 240</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Zufügung <hi rend="italic">regis</hi> zu Q soll wohl ‘staatlich’ heissen, im Ggs. zur privaten Fehde der Barone im 12. Jh.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The addition of <hi rend="italic">regis</hi> in Q is probably meant to signify ‘of the state’, in contrast to the private feuds of the barons in the 12th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">homicidium</hi> Hn 80,1; so Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk</hi>. 94. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Halbverletzung, auch o. I 2, 3 gegen 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">homicidium</hi> Hn 80,1; so Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk</hi>. 94. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Halbverletzung, also above I 2, 3 as against 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_61.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">210</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Friedlosigkeit bei Alemannen; Brunner II 583</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Outlawry among the Alamans; Brunner II 583</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_61.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘perpetrates to the full a breach of the peace,’ <hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> probably, by committing homicide.</seg></note>
      </div>
